1233
00:45:27,040 --> 00:45:31,920
deeper, shallower, wider, or narrower to

1234
00:45:29,839 --> 00:45:33,920
control the resolution and sensitivity

1235
00:45:31,920 --> 00:45:36,079
of the measurement.

1236
00:45:33,920 --> 00:45:37,920
By analyzing how the returned echoes

1237
00:45:36,079 --> 00:45:39,839
shift over time, we can extract

1238
00:45:37,920 --> 00:45:43,800
information about both motion and flow

1239
00:45:39,839 --> 00:45:43,800
at that specific location.

1240
00:45:45,440 --> 00:45:49,760
Let's imagine we send a pulse to a

1241
00:45:47,280 --> 00:45:52,079
stationary target, say a student sitting

1242
00:45:49,760 --> 00:45:55,119
still. The pulse travels to that target

1243
00:45:52,079 --> 00:45:57,040
and comes back after a certain time.

1244
00:45:55,119 --> 00:45:58,560
Suppose it takes exactly 100

1245
